'''Sa'Kalla''' was a young [[Drabatan]] [[Musician|singer]] who spoke out against the [[Galactic Empire]]'s tyranny by [[1 BBY]]. In retaliation, the Empire [[blockade]]d her [[Homeworld|home planet]] of [[Pipada]] and held her in [[Prisoner|captivity]], where she was [[torture]]d. A [[Sa'Kalla (movement)|movement]] was organized in her name that opposed the Empire. As the movement began to threaten the Imperial occupation, Sa'Kalla was brought to the [[Pipada Auditorium]] by the [[Unidentified Imperial governor (Pipada)|Imperial governor]]. There, she urged her people to continue fighting before she was quickly [[Death|killed]] on stage in front of the crowd. Her death inspired the Drabatans to rise up against the Empire.

==Biography==
===Songs of freedom===
[[File:Imperial_Emblem.svg|thumb|right|200px|Sa'Kalla spoke out against the Galactic Empire.]]
Sa'Kalla was a young [[Drabatan]] [[Musician|singer]] who lived on the Drabatan [[homeworld]]<ref name="Dawn" />&mdash;the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]]<ref name="Galaxy Map">[[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]]</ref> [[planet]] [[Pipada]]&mdash;during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Dawn" /> By [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> she wrote popular protest songs condemning the [[Galactic Empire]]'s tyranny and become one of its most vocal opponents, which quickly reached the Imperials. The Empire responded by conducting a [[crackdown on Pipada]] and [[Blockade|blockading]] the planet, deploying [[garrison]]s of [[swamptrooper]]s to its surface.<ref name="Dawn" />

Sa'Kalla was [[Prisoner|captured]] and [[torture]]d. While she was held, a [[Sa'Kalla (movement)|movement]] was organized in her name, and as it threatened to overwhelm the Imperial occupation, Sa'Kalla was brought to the [[Pipada Auditorium]] by the planet's [[Unidentified Imperial governor (Pipada)|Imperial governor]] in front of half a million Drabatans. The Empire believed they had broken her through torture and ordered her to convince her people to submit to Imperial rule. Instead, Sa'Kalla defiantly shouted to her people that they should continue to resist the Empire before being immediately [[Death|killed]] on stage. The enraged Drabatans, incensed by her death, tore apart the Imperial security forces present in the auditorium.<ref name="Dawn" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|Drabatans are freshwater amphibiods, so the salt water on Scarif was unpleasent for Pao. He nevertheless charged into battle with his Drabatese war cry of 'Sa'kalla!' against his Imperial enemies, inspiring his many squad mates to follow suit.|A section of the entry on Drabatans in an artist's journal|<ref name="Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref>}}
[[File:PaoCover.png|thumb|left|200px|Drabatans such as Pao (pictured) used Sa'Kalla's name as a battle cry.]]
As a result of Sa'Kalla's cries for rebellion, the Drabatans briefly retook their homeworld while many fled offworld. Despite their efforts, the Empire returned to Pipada, taking over with heavy reinforcements and imposing martial law across the planet. The Drabatan people adopted Sa'Kalla's name as a war cry as they charged into battle.<ref name="Dawn" /> One such Drabatan was the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[commando]] [[Paodok'Draba'Takat Sap'De'Rekti Nik'Linke'Ti' Ki'Vef'Nik'NeSevef'Li'Kek|Paodok'Draba'Takat]], who shouted her name during the [[Battle of Scarif]]<ref name="Ultimate Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> in 1 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>

Sa'Kalla was remembered [[Standard year|years]] later through Paodok'Draba'Takat's use of her name in his battle cry, which was included in an [[Unidentified artist's journal|artist's journal]] written<ref name="Archive" /> no earlier than [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref> The battle cry was included as part of an entry on the Drabatan species. The journal eventually came into the possession of the [[Graf Archive]]&mdash;a vast depository owned by the [[Graf family]] that contained documents that held historical importance.<ref name="Archive" />

==Behind the scenes==
Sa'Kalla was first mentioned in a battle cry in the [[Star Wars Anthology Series|Anthology Series]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''<ref name="Rogue One" /> alongside [[Pablo Hidalgo]]'s reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''<ref name="Ultimate Guide" /> and [[Jason Fry]]'s young-readers book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Secret Mission]]'',<ref name="Secret Mission">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Secret Mission]]''</ref> which were released simultaneously on [[December 16]], [[2016]].<ref name="Rebel Reading">{{SW|url=news/rebel-reading-rogue-one-books|text=Rebel Reading: A Guide to ''Rogue One'' Books}}</ref> Sa'Kalla was then established as an individual and identified in ''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]'', a [[2018]] [[Roleplaying game|roleplaying]] sourcebook published by [[Fantasy Flight Games]] for the ''[[Star Wars Roleplaying]]'' game.<ref name="Dawn" />

